{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774727,"nonce":"BW/p6hCLyhN86Wj2uHSW9T9T2C4=","title":"docs: ADR-0059 (Proposed) — per-run scheduler-tick fault isolation","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #53 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `docs/adr-0059-tick-fault-isolation` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-21T17:12:51Z · Merged: 2026-07-21T17:35:58Z\n\nA **Proposed** ADR to discuss the follow-up work surfaced by ADR-0058's \"Fix B\" (in PR #52).\n\nFix B made `reconcile_services` per-run fault-isolated in the scheduler tick, but it's a *point fix*, not the general property:\n1. **`admit` and `advance` still `?`-abort the whole tick** — one Run's error there still stalls every other Run that cycle.\n2. **Swallowed per-Run errors retry forever, unbounded** — great for transient/fixable errors (self-heal), but a *persistent* per-Run error hot-loops with no dead-letter, brushing the \"forward progress **or** explicit dead-letter\" invariant (CONTEXT §7.1) — the same gap Fix A closed for service *launch* errors.\n\n1. **Per-Run fault isolation as a tick invariant** — isolate `admit`/`advance` too; one poison Run can never stall the fleet. Engine stays pure (returns the collected errors; the driver logs).\n2. **Tick-global failures stay fatal** (outer `Result`); per-Run poison is isolated (inner `Vec`).\n3. **Bound persistent per-Run failures → dead-letter**, preferring a wall-clock deadline (consistent with Fix A) over a tick-count.\n\nIncludes explicit **open questions** (bound mechanism, where the durable failure signal lives, cross-run passes, multi-replica interaction, ADR-0047 classification) — this is a discussion doc, not a decided design. No code changes.\n\nFollow-up to #52 (ADR-0058); git-bug 6825830.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}